<title>ITALY: Italy's Cariplo H1 1996 net profit up 26.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Italy's Cariplo H1 1996 net profit up 26.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Milan-based savings bank Cariplo reported net profits of 189 billion lire in the first half of 1996, showing a rise of 26.8 percent compared to the first half of 1995.</p>
<p>A group statement added that first half profit net of tax was 286 billion lire, up 9.3 percent, while the gross profit was up 8.3 percent at 384 billion lire.</p>
<p>Net interest income slipped 0.2 percent to 2.378 trillion lire, while operating income rose 8.4 percent to 3.453 trillion.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
